I also wish to become a member of the Logical Language Group. I believe
that because I've begun and continued to use Lojban very much that my
membership would be good for Lojban. Bob or others have said or thought (I
suppose), respectively, that the Logical Language Group should concern
itself only with organization. However, I believe that the members of LLG
should be proficient lojbanists. What else but skill can be necessary to
the development and promotion of Lojban? (Rhetorical question, and I am
slightly exaggerating, but that requirement still holds.)

Jacob

